      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Montreal artist Geneviève Letarte is the author of several novels, of which “Soleil Rauque” (“Hoarse Sun”) was the most acclaimed. She also published a collection of poetry, and has recorded two albums of songs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Biographical Context"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "fffbe882-4856-4ef4-9e85-109cde925cb6"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 77,
      "end_time": 77,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "During her performance she sings through window drapes hanging on a rod over her head, which she pushes apart, to be seen."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "9bd5e419-31d1-4ec7-bc49-c17914032162"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 165,
      "end_time": 165,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The musicians accompanying her are: Bernard Poirier: Guitar, bass, percussion, and Claude Saint-Jean: Synthesizer, trombone."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
